>h1 Cupid toolchain workers

Mount the compiler source ISO at /src. Run the staged worker ELF with exec.

>h2 Compile a source

Place two LF-terminated lines in /home/cupidc.job. The first names the
source relative to the ISO root. The second names the output under /home.

  /toolchain/ctool.cc
  /home/ctool.o

>h2 Link objects

Place the output, text base, entry symbol and object paths in
/home/cupidld.job. Put one field or path on each line. Object order
matches the link order.

  /home/hello.elf
  0x01c00000
  _start
  /home/hello.o

Use 0x01c00000 for an ordinary executable and 0x01e00000 for a compiler
worker. Each worker returns to the shell after reporting its result.
Wait for its lease to be released before starting another worker.
Both workers release cached work buffers before publishing output and
again when the job ends.

>h2 Assemble a relocatable object

  as -f elf32 -o /home/start.o /home/start.asm

The assembler gives .rodata four-byte default alignment. CupidLD places
the bytes in a read-only ELF segment and resolves references to its labels.
